Recently, I donated a large amount of gold to a priestess of Rat God
(while being chaotic), and she bestowed on me a blessing.  This seems
to take the form of clairvoyance -- I can sense nearby walls,
corridors, etc.  Which is really useful once you get to the maze
levels.  Problem is, it goes away.  At first, I thought it was only
going away the next time I interacted with my god, which really sucked,
but then I realized that there seemed to be a time constraint involved.
Which also sucks, because it's a really cool ability, and there aren't
that many temples.  Can anyone tell me more?

Also, I have Stormbringer -- got it on the third level or so, and my
god gave me "Hand of Elbereth" on a later level, with the whole message
about taking souls for whoever, and an unnamed wide sword appeared at
my feet.  I left it there, because I already had Stormbringer.  Is the
game actually smart enough to know that there can only be one
Stormbringer?  Was the sword any better than a normal broadsword?







